{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Everyday Things", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "How Often Does She Work?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "Beginner", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Asking Questions with When", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " When is the class? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You ask questions with <span class=\"strong\"> When</span> to know the time, day or date of an activity. <br/> <span class=\"strong\"> When</span> is the first word in the question. <br/>It is followed by the verb <span class=\"strong\"> to be</span> or a form of <span class=\"strong\"> do</span>.<br/><br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When + verb to be + subject ... ?<br />When + do/does + subject + verb ... ?<br/><br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When do you start yoga?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When does your class finish?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When are the rooms open?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When does the library open?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Asking Questions with How Often and How Long", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">James:</span> How often does your sister swim? </br> <span class=\"strong\"> Alex:</span> Once a week. <br/><span class=\"strong\">James:</span> How often do you swim?</span> </br><span class=\"strong\"> Alex:</span> Twice a week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You ask <span class=\"strong\"> How often</span> to know the frequency of an activity.<br/> You ask<span class=\"strong\">  How long</span> to know the duration of an activity. <br/>These words are followed by <span class=\"strong\"> do </span> or <span class=\"strong\"> does </span> or the verb  <span class=\"strong\"> to be</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">James:</span> How long is the class?</span> </br><span class=\"strong\"> Alex:</span> The class is 1 hour long.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "activity", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a thing that a person or group does", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Yoga is a new activity for me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when talking about activities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "yoga", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a form of body movement and meditation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I like yoga. I do it often.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "every day", "type": "name"}, {"content": "each day; daily", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sarah goes to work every day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "How long ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "question asking for duration of time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(pronoun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How long is the class?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "It's __ long", "type": "name"}, {"content": "Expression used to talk about the duration of an activity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"strong\">A:</